# reels2Claude configuration
#
# Where to put your real settings (never commit them):
#   - Installed plugin:            ~/.reels2claude/.env   (Windows: %USERPROFILE%\.reels2claude\.env)
#   - Working on this repo itself: .env in the repo root (already gitignored)
# Real environment variables always win over these files.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Transcription: turn the reel's speech into text.
#    Default: local whisper.cpp (free, private, nothing is uploaded).
#    If it isn't installed, the first API with a key is used: Groq -> OpenAI -> Gemini.
#    If an API fails, whisper.cpp is used instead when it's installed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local whisper.cpp (default, no key needed). A ggml-*.bin model in
# ~/.reels2claude/models/ is found automatically; set these only to use a model
# or binary somewhere else.
# WHISPER_CPP_BIN=/path/to/whisper-cli
# WHISPER_CPP_MODEL=/path/to/ggml-small.bin

# Optional online APIs. To use one even though whisper.cpp is installed,
# also set REELS2CLAUDE_PROVIDER (below).
# Groq -> https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# OpenAI (paid, about $0.006 per minute of audio) -> https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini -> https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Force a specific provider instead of auto-detect: local | groq | openai | gemini | none
# REELS2CLAUDE_PROVIDER=

# Override the provider's default model (advanced)
# REELS2CLAUDE_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) Instagram login walls (OFF by default)
#    Lets the downloader borrow your browser's login cookies. Firefox works most
#    reliably; recent Chrome versions on Windows often block this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REELS2CLAUDE_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER=firefox

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Tool locations, only if they are installed somewhere unusual
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YTDLP_PATH=
# FFMPEG_PATH=
# FFPROBE_PATH=
